        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "*As a* Shopper, \n*I want* to see a consistent global header on every page, \n*so that* I can always access key navigation and account features regardless of where I am on the site.\n\nReference image (Figma is leading):\n\n!image-20260618-040938.png|width=922,alt=\"image-20260618-040938.png\"!\n\n----\n\nThe global header is a sticky component displayed at the top of every page across all storefronts and devices. It contains the Zimmermann logo, header icons, {color:#ff5630}and country/region selector for non-AU sites.{color} The header remains visible as the shopper scrolls down the page.\n\nThis story covers the *header shell and layout only* — the visual structure, component placement, and sticky behaviour. Icon destinations (Search, Account, Wish List, Cart) are wired up as the underlying pages and features are built in their respective stories. The exception is the logo (links to homepage).\n\n*Header elements:*\n\n* *Zimmermann logo/wordmark* — centred in the header, links back to the homepage on click\n* *Navigation menu -* based on the latest Figma design, top-level categories include: NEW, CLOTHING, ACCESSORIES, COLLECTIONS, Z.IMMERSE. For this user story, we can create this structure and for now and create Contentful placeholders if possible. We can populate sample values if Contentful is not available.\n* *Header icons (right-aligned):* Search, Account, Bag, Wishlist, Bag; displayed as visual elements - destination page in other stories.\n* *Bag icon* — displays a running count of items currently in the shopper's bag \n* {color:#ff5630}*Country/region selector*{color}{color:#ff5630} — displayed in the header on all storefronts except AU; allows shoppers to switch their region and currency. Persists the selected region across sessions.{color}\n\n*Responsive behaviour:* There is a header design for both desktop and mobile.",
          "to_string": "*As a* Shopper, \n*I want* to see a consistent global header on every page, \n*so that* I can always access key navigation and account features regardless of where I am on the site.\n\nReference image (Figma is leading):\n\n!image-20260618-040938.png|width=922,alt=\"image-20260618-040938.png\"!\n\n----\n\nThe global header is a sticky component displayed at the top of every page across all storefronts and devices. It contains the Zimmermann logo, header icons, {color:#ff5630}and country/region selector for non-AU sites.{color} The header remains visible as the shopper scrolls down the page.\n\nThis story covers the *header shell and layout only* — the visual structure, component placement, and sticky behaviour. Icon destinations (Search, Account, Wish List, Cart) are wired up as the underlying pages and features are built in their respective stories. The exception is the logo (links to homepage).\n\n*Header elements:*\n\n* *Zimmermann logo/wordmark* — centred in the header, links back to the homepage on click\n* *Navigation menu -* based on the latest Figma design, top-level categories include: NEW, CLOTHING, ACCESSORIES, COLLECTIONS, Z.IMMERSE. For this user story, we will set up the first basis of the navigation items in SFCC.\n* *Header icons (right-aligned):* Search, Account, Bag, Wishlist, Bag; displayed as visual elements - destination page in other stories.\n* *Bag icon* — displays a running count of items currently in the shopper's bag \n* {color:#ff5630}*Country/region selector*{color}{color:#ff5630} — displayed in the header on all storefronts except AU; allows shoppers to switch their region and currency. Persists the selected region across sessions.{color}\n\n*Responsive behaviour:* There is a header design for both desktop and mobile."
        }
      ],
