        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "# Given a shopper visits any page on the storefront, when the page loads, then the global header is displayed at the top of the page on both desktop and mobile.\n# Given a shopper scrolls down the page, when the page is scrolled, then the header remains sticky and visible at the top of the screen.\n# Given a shopper clicks the Zimmermann logo, when the click is registered, then the shopper is navigated to the homepage.\n# Given a shopper views the header, when the page loads, then all header icons (Search, Account, Bag, Wishlist, Bag) are visible per the linked Figma Design.\n# Given a shopper has items in their bag, when they view the header, then the Bag icon displays the correct running count of items.\n# Given a bag item is added or removed, when the bag is updated, then the Bag icon count updates without requiring a full page reload.\n# {color:#ff5630}Given a shopper is on any storefront except AU, when they view the header, then the country/region selector is visible.{color}\n# {color:#ff5630}Given a shopper is on the AU storefront, when they view the header, then no country/region selector is displayed.{color}",
          "to_string": "# Given a shopper visits any page on the storefront, when the page loads, then the global header is displayed at the top of the page on both desktop and mobile.\n# Given a shopper scrolls down the page, when the page is scrolled, then the header remains sticky and visible at the top of the screen.\n# Given a shopper clicks the Zimmermann logo, when the click is registered, then the shopper is navigated to the homepage.\n# Given a shopper views the header, when the page loads, then all header icons (Search, Account, Bag, Wishlist, Bag) are visible per the linked Figma Design.\n# Given a shopper has items in their bag, when they view the header, then the Bag icon displays the correct running count of items.\n# Given a bag item is added or removed, when the bag is updated, then the Bag icon count updates without requiring a full page reload.\n# Given a shopper views the site on mobile, when any page loads, then the hamburger icon is displayed top-left in the header alongside Search and Bag icons top-right.\n# Given a shopper taps the hamburger icon, when the tap is registered, then the full-screen navigation drawer opens and the hamburger icon is replaced by a close (×) icon.\n# Given the navigation drawer is open, when a shopper taps the close (×) icon, then the drawer closes and the hamburger icon is restored.\n# Given the navigation drawer is open, when a shopper views it, then all top-level navigation categories are displayed vertically in the correct order per the linked Figma design.\n# Given the navigation drawer is open, when a shopper views it, then Saved and Account links are displayed below the main navigation categories.\n# {color:#ff5630}Given a shopper is on any storefront except AU, when they view the header, then the country/region selector is visible.{color}\n# {color:#ff5630}Given a shopper is on the AU storefront, when they view the header, then no country/region selector is displayed.{color}",
          "from_id": "",
          "to_id": ""
        }
      ],
