          "to_string": "*As a* Shopper, \n*I want* to see a consistent global header on every page, \n*so that* I can always access key navigation and account features regardless of where I am on the site.\n\nReference image (Figma is leading):\n\n!image-20260618-040346.png|width=922,alt=\"image-20260618-040346.png\"!\n\n----\n\nThe global header is a sticky component displayed at the top of every page across all storefronts and devices. It contains the Zimmermann logo, header icons, and country/region selector. The header remains visible as the shopper scrolls down the page.\n\nThis story covers the *header shell and layout only* — the visual structure, component placement, and sticky behaviour. Icon destinations (Wishlist, Account, Search, Locate Boutique, Contact Us, Newsletter) are wired up as the underlying pages and features are built in their respective stories. The exception is the logo (links to homepage)\n\n*Header elements:*\n\n* *Zimmermann logo/wordmark* — centred in the header, links back to the homepage on click\n* *Header icons (right-aligned):* Search, Account, Bag, Wishlist, Locate Boutique, Contact Us, Newsletter; displayed as visual elements\n* *Bag icon* — displays a running count of items currently in the shopper's bag \n* {color:#ff5630}*Country/region selector*{color}{color:#ff5630} — displayed in the header on all storefronts except AU; allows shoppers to switch their region and currency. Persists the selected region across sessions.{color}\n* *Navigation menu* is covered in another user story.\n\n*Responsive behaviour:* There is a header design for both desktop and mobile."
        }
