          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "*As a* Shopper,\n\n*I want* to see a consistent headline navigation on every page,\n\n*so that* I can access top-level site categories and key account actions regardless of where I am on the site.\n\n----\n\nThis is a *PWA Kit component story*. It covers the build of the {{Navigation}} React component in the PWA Kit storefront — the headline nav bar that renders on every page across all storefronts and devices.\n\nThe {{Navigation}} component was initially built as part of SFCC-52 (Global Header UI), which focused on the visual structure and placement of the headline nav items. That story was in build before the new component approach was developed. This story supersedes the navigation portion of SFCC-52 and defines the full {{Navigation}} component at the headline level.\n\nTop-level nav items and their ordering are driven by the SFCC category taxonomy configured in Business Manager (SFCC-28), not hardcoded in the component. Mega menu behaviour on desktop is covered in SFCC-96. Mobile hamburger and drill-down behaviour is covered in SFCC-97. The following are also explicitly out of scope: logo (SFCC-52), scroll animation/motion (SFCC-93), country and currency selector (SFCC-79), icon link destinations (respective feature stories), and hover/focus/active visual states (defined in UI kit).",
          "to_string": "*As a* Shopper,\n\n*I want* to see a consistent headline navigation on every page,\n\n*so that* I can access top-level site categories and key account actions regardless of where I am on the site.\n\n----\n\nThis is a *PWA Kit component story*. It covers the build of the {{Navigation}} React component in the PWA Kit storefront — the headline nav bar that renders on every page across all storefronts and devices.\n\nThe {{Navigation}} component was initially built as part of SFCC-52 [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-52|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-52|smart-link] , which focused on the visual structure and placement of the headline nav items. That story was in build before the new component approach was developed. This story supersedes the navigation portion of [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-52|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-52|smart-link]  and defines the full {{Navigation}} component at the headline level.\n\nTop-level nav items and their ordering are driven by the SFCC category taxonomy configured in Business Manager ([https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-28|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-28|smart-link] ), not hardcoded in the component. Mega menu behaviour on desktop is covered in [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-96|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-96|smart-link] . Mobile hamburger and drill-down behaviour is covered in [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-97|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-97|smart-link] .\n\nThe following are also explicitly out of scope: hover/focus/active visual states (defined in UI kit)."
        }
